**Reasoning:**
- The 4th ordering (pressure × size descending) captures a different heuristic dimension than density (pressure/size), giving the greedy more chances to find a low-max-KVPR arrangement.
- The swap refinement addresses cases where a pure move can't help (e.g., all other GPUs are too full to accept a model, but an exchange can rebalance pressure). It only recurses when a strict improvement is found, so it terminates quickly and adds negligible time relative to the 360s budget.
- The `_greedy` returns `None` on infeasibility instead of raising inside the loop, so other orderings still get tried; the error is raised only if all orderings fail.
